# /etc/inittab - mpos (aarch64): a getty on the console and on the virtual consoles
#
# The same shape as the x86_64 machine's `/etc/inittab` - openrc's three
# runlevels, then a getty respawning on each virtual console - plus one line the
# x86_64 file does not carry, and the difference is a fact about the two
# machines rather than a preference.
#
# `tty1`..`tty4` are the virtual consoles. On x86_64 a getty there is visible on
# the serial wire because the kernel's console multiplexer carries each console's
# bytes over it (`vcmux`); this machine has no multiplexer yet, so those lines are
# the parity target that is *not* satisfied - a getty starts on each and its
# output has nowhere to go until that port lands (`PLAN.md` §13's next unit).
#
# `ttyAMA0` is this machine's console: the PL011, whose name the psABI gives the
# first serial port on aarch64 and which `/dev` publishes under exactly that
# name. A getty there is what makes the boot reachable - it is where the login
# prompt appears, and it is also what a stock serial-console Alpine does. The
# x86_64 image leaves its own `ttyS0` without a getty because its console is
# already reachable through the virtual consoles above.

::sysinit:/sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc default

ttyAMA0::respawn:/sbin/getty -L 38400 ttyAMA0 vt100

tty1::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty1
tty2::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty2
tty3::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty3
tty4::respawn:/sbin/getty 38400 tty4

# Stuff to do for the 3-finger salute
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot

# Stuff to do before rebooting
::shutdown:/sbin/openrc shutdown
